        <BoQCtgy ID="C4" RNoPart="2">
          <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Civil works-other work</span><br/></LblTx>
          <BoQBody>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C5" RNoPart="1">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Documentation civil works total BA 01 + BA 02</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Item ID="I33" RNoPart="1">
                    <LumpSumItem>Yes</LumpSumItem>
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation of the essential construction sequence,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">in particular to show the design of individual construction parts and structure parts that are later no longer visible and testable, produce with digital camera and hand over to the AG.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photos are to be collected in a system ordered by topics, including tables of contents with the details  (structure, date, location details) of the pictures shown.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Digital document in PDF format</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photos in JPEG format (image size min. 900x600 pixels)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photo documentation is to be handed over to the AG 2 weeks before acceptance digitally for checking on CD - 2 copies:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Prepare photo documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I34" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">hand over as additional copy  on CD.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation as PDF file incl. photos as JPEG file, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billed is one set of the photo documentation in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply photo documentation on data carrier CD</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I35" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">in [PERSON_097], collected in folders, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The content of the folders is to be broken down ordered by topics;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">A table of contents is to be placed in front of the content</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spines are to be labelled according to the specification of the AG.The labelling of the folder spines is specified uniformly for the entire project.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billed is one set of the documentation in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply photo documentation in [PERSON_097]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I36" RNoPart="4">
                    <LumpSumItem>Yes</LumpSumItem>
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Prepare as-built documents of all work carried out on the basis of the updated execution design.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The AN has to survey the lines and structures laid and found in the course of the digging works </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; text-decoration:underline; font-family:Arial">continuously</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"> digitally. The necessary surveying works as well as local  measurements are to be included in the price and are not paid separately.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The drawing documents must be prepared in digital form  and marked as [PERSON_118], contain the scale and if applicable be provided with a revision note.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The following contents must be shown:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Position and level of the structures built</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Line plan including</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">  nominal diameters, gradient profile, invert levels</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Invert and cover levels of the shaft structures</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Finished levels</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- the indication of all built-in components in the UTM coordinate system</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">  with indication of the coordinates for position and level</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Furthermore all technical drawings or detail drawings used are to be handed over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">When incorporating and preparing the [PERSON_118] the layer structures acc. to the design handed over by the AG are to be retained.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Structure of the as-built documentation:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Table of contents</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- [PERSON_118]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Layer list</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- List with assignment of the line colours to the line widths</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The design is made available to the AN for further processing as</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">CAD file in DWG format.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The as-built documents are to be handed over to the AG 2 weeks before acceptance digitally for checking on CD - 2 copies:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">CAD drawing in DWG or DXF format</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">other drawing documents in format PDF format</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Prepare as-built documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I37" RNoPart="5">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">As-built documents </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">hand over as additional copy  on CD.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billed is one set of the photo documentation in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply as-built documentation on data carrier CD</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I38" RNoPart="6">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_097]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">, collected in folders, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The content of the folders is to be broken down ordered by topics;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">A table of contents is to be placed in front of the content</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spines are to be labelled according to the specification of the AG.The labelling of the folder spines is specified uniformly for the entire project.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billed is one set of the documentation in each case..</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply as-built documentation in [PERSON_097]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
        <BoQCtgy ID="C6" RNoPart="3">
          <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Civil works-[PERSON_132] [PERSON_151]. East - main route 2023</span><br/></LblTx>
          <BoQBody>
            <Remark ID="R3">
              <Description>
                <CompleteText>
                  <DetailTxt>
                    <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Sensitive facilities in the surroundings of the site, possible restrictions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Between central workshop and Immerwahrstraße there is the institute building "IZNF". </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On the ground floor and partly in the basement of this building, on the north side </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">measuring rooms with highly sensitive measuring instruments and microscopes are set up, with which </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">experiments are carried out that tolerate no vibrations.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">For this reason, for compaction works, compaction equipment is always </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be used that works with low vibration owing to its vibration frequency; </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">excitation frequency &gt; 40 Hz.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Before the start of the construction measure a construction schedule is to be prepared by the AN, from which the </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">approximate times for the vibration-prone works are evident.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On the basis of this construction schedule, coordination is then carried out with the responsible supervisor of the measuring facilities in the IZNF, in order to fix a time schedule acceptable to all sides for vibration-free times and times in which vibration-prone works can be carried out. The vibration-prone works are therefore to be announced with a lead time of at least 2 weeks at the IZNF, via the [FIRMA_001] and the construction supervision. The vibration-prone construction works so far in the immediate surroundings of the IZNF could, according to experience, be carried out without problems after coordination.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                  </DetailTxt>
                  <OutlineText>
                    <OutlTxt>
                      <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Low-vibration construction equipment, excitation frequency &gt; 40 Hz, poss. restrictions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                    </OutlTxt>
                  </OutlineText>
                </CompleteText>
              </Description>
            </Remark>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C7" RNoPart="1">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Site preparation and development</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R4">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Demolition, removal</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Demolition, removal</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
