                      <CompleteText>
                        <ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Demolition of the kerb of concrete, as part of a partial demolition measure, shape TB 10/25, incl. foundation of concrete and one-sided backing support, bedding thickness 20 cm, thickness of the backing support 10 cm, unit weight of the demolition material DIN EN 1991-1-1 24 kN/m3, use of equipment is possible, max. total weight up to 20 t, execution low-vibration DIN 4150, low-noise, noise level max. 80 dB(A), </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">collect materials taken up, load onto truck of the AN, transport, dispose of, to the storage/to the facility according to [PERSON_125] of the AN, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                          <TextComplement Kind="Bidder" MarkLbl="11" ArtChrIdent="-43">
                            <ComplCaption><span>Facility (designation/location) </span></ComplCaption>
                            <ComplBody><span/><br/><span/><br/><span>  .......................... </span></ComplBody>
                            <ComplTail><span>to be entered by the bidder</span></ComplTail>
                          </TextComplement>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be entered by the bidder,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">waste is not hazardous, not contaminated, classification Z 0 (unrestricted installation), waste code acc. to AVV (Waste Catalogue Ordinance) 170101 concrete, quantity determination by measurement, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment for the disposal is borne by AN.</span></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Demolish kerb concrete TB10/25 24kN/m3 equipment use poss. load transp. truck AN dispose of not contaminated AVV170101 paym.disposal AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I40" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>85</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Removal of the kerb of concrete for later reuse, as part of a partial demolition measure, shape TB 10/25, clean removed kerb and store at the side on pallets for later reinstallation.  Demolish foundation of concrete and one-sided backing support, bedding thickness 20 cm, thickness of the backing support 10 cm, unit weight of the demolition material DIN EN 1991-1-1 24 kN/m3, use of equipment is possible, max. total weight up to 20 t, execution low-vibration DIN 4150, low-noise, noise level max. 80 dB(A), sort materials taken up for disposal, collect, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">load onto truck of the AN, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">collect materials taken up, load onto truck of the AN, transport, dispose of, to the storage/to the facility according to [PERSON_125] of the AN, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                          <TextComplement Kind="Bidder" MarkLbl="11" ArtChrIdent="-1">
                            <ComplCaption><span>Facility (designation/location) </span></ComplCaption>
                            <ComplBody><span/><br/><span/><br/><span>  .......................... </span></ComplBody>
                            <ComplTail><span/></ComplTail>
                          </TextComplement>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be entered by the bidder,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">waste is not hazardous, not contaminated, classification Z 0 (unrestricted installation), waste code acc. to AVV (Waste Catalogue Ordinance) 170101 concrete, quantity determination by measurement, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment for the disposal is borne by AN.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Removal kerb concrete for reuse TB10/25 24kN/m3 equipment use poss. TB10/25 24kN/m3, load transp. truck AN dispose of not contaminated AVV170101 paym.disposal </span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I41" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>400</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Take up existing paving, [PERSON_083] in rows, clean and store at the side on pallets for reuse, in areas beside the carriageway, as part of a partial demolition measure.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Execution low-noise, noise level max. 80 dB(A).</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Quantity determination by measurement.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Width of area taken up:  over 2,5 to 4,0 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Type of paving: [PERSON_083], in rows</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Thickness: 100 mm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Take up [PERSON_083] for reuse, rows, D 100mm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
