                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Locate existing cables in the site area before the start of construction by means of a cable locator and mark them on site.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Low-voltage cables and medium-voltage cables</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Obtain the as-built drawing documents in advance from the responsible utility companies and line owners.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Enter located cables in the handed-over working drawings or site plan with reference dimensions to existing buildings.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billing by size of the locating area (length of the single construction route x width of the construction route).</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Cable locating low and medium voltage, marking</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
