            <BoQCtgy ID="C11" RNoPart="5">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Hourly-rate work civil works [PERSON_132] + well water pipeline 2023</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R18">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work (daywork)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work (daywork)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="R19">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Carrying out hourly-rate work against proof and at the request of the local site management. Work is paid if its execution was ordered in writing by the site management.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Only the working hours actually performed for personnel and equipment are charged. If a special [PERSON_037] is kept for the work, no payment is granted for the supervisory personnel, unless expressly agreed otherwise beforehand.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Insofar as hourly charge rates claimed are not contained in the bid, the contractor is obliged at the client's request to furnish proof of the actual labour costs on the basis of the payroll lists.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Wages above the collective agreement and ancillary labour costs are to be proven to the client on request.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surcharges on the charge rates for night, Sunday,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">public holiday and additional work (overtime) ordered by the client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">or for which the client is responsible are</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be proven separately; they are paid in the amount of the collective</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">agreement. For night, Sunday and public holiday work, only the contribution to statutory accident insurance is paid as a surcharge. For additional work, the social costs are additionallypaid.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">All surcharges such as overheads, social contributions, accommodation allowance, travel money etc. are to be included in the hourly rate. Billing is against proof. The daywork sheets are to be signed daily by the building owner, as otherwise the wage work will not be recognised. Billing with the client has to take place promptly.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The bid total of the hourly-rate work is included in the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">bid evaluation, the hourly-rate work is</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">however not commissioned. The hourly rates offered</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">become part of the contract.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The contractor has no claim to the consumption of the hours provided for; the same charge rates apply to more or fewer hours performed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I90" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <RefDescr>Ref</RefDescr>
                    <Qty>80</Qty>
                    <QU>h</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <STLBBau>
                        <STLBBauCtlg>
                          <CtlgName>STLB-Bau</CtlgName>
                          <VersDate>2020-04</VersDate>
                          <WCtg>091</WCtg>
                          <Group>1619</Group>
                        </STLBBauCtlg>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>2136</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>39</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>9088</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>80</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>11100</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>1</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>10164</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>1</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work by skilled construction worker (m/f) </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the charge-out rate for the respective worker covers all expenses such as wage and salary costs, ancillary wage and salary costs, supplements, wage-bound and wage-dependent costs, other social costs, overheads, risk and profit.</span></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Skilled construction worker (m/f) all costs/surcharges</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I91" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <RefDescr>Rep</RefDescr>
                    <RefRNo IDRef="I90"/>
                    <Qty>60</Qty>
                    <QU>h</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Construction labourer (m/f)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Construction labourer (m/f)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="R20">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dewatering</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">According to the soil report, the groundwater occurs below the base of the subsoil. In order to intercept any [PERSON_149] that may occur, the bill of quantities contains work for dewatering. The [PERSON_029] that may have to be pumped off can be pumped on the east side of Immerwahrstraße into an infiltration basin north of the IZNF building. Under this infiltration basin there is an infiltration trench for the infiltration of precipitation water.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dewatering</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I92" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Set up, clear submersible pump for dewatering; including electrical supply line and hose line for discharge into existing infiltration basin.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pump type:  electric motor</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Delivery rate: 10-30m3/h</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Delivery head:  up to 5m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hose line: approx. 100 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pump electric motor 10-30m3/h h up to 5m set up, clear, hose line 100 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I93" RNoPart="4">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>5</Qty>
                    <QU>d</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Keep available on site and operate submersible pump for dewatering from previous item; including electrical supply line and hose line for discharge into existing infiltration basin;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billing by days of use</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pump electric motor 10-30m3/h h up to 5m keep available on site, operate</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I94" RNoPart="5">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Construct and clear pump sump within the excavation pit from excavation base, of concrete well rings, clear diameter 1000 mm, depth up to 1 m, execution according to </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Incl. gravel filter.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pump sump construct clear concrete well ring DN1000 T up to 1m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="R21">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control tests</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control tests</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="R22">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control tests - preliminary remarks</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The control tests listed in this section do not replace the tests which the contractor must perform according to the relevant guidelines for monitoring his work as part of self-monitoring and whose results are also to be handed over to the client in copy.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The control services listed below are only to be caried out on the order of the AG.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control tests - preliminary remarks</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I95" RNoPart="6">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>10</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control test ZTV E-StB on special order of the AG for subgrade/formation, test for deformation modulus, with dynamic plate load test TP BF-StB. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On special order of the AG for the degree of compaction of the fills to check the self-monitoring of the AN. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Calibrated test device is to be provided by the AN.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control test subgrade/formation deformation modulus </span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">dynamic plate load test</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I96" RNoPart="7">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>10</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On special order of the AG to check the self-monitoring of the AN. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Medium-heavy dynamic probe acc. to DIN 4094 (tip cross-section 15 cm2), incl. travel to and from site or setting up and keeping available on site. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The probing is to be carried out jointly with the construction supervision of the AG.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dynamic probing DIN EN ISO 22476-2, for in-situ determination of the resistance of soils and soft rock to the dynamic penetration of a probe tip, termination criterion: number of blows up to 10 cm penetration depth: 3 times consecutively greater than 30 or number of blows up to 10 cm penetration depth: once greater than 90, heavy dynamic probing (DPH), drilling depth up to 5 m.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dynamic probing DPH</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
        <BoQCtgy ID="C12" RNoPart="4">
          <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Civil works-well water pipeline 2023</span><br/></LblTx>
          <BoQBody>
            <Remark ID="R23">
              <Description>
                <CompleteText>
                  <DetailTxt>
                    <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Sensitive facilities in the surroundings of the site, possible restrictions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Between central workshop and Immerwahrstraße there is the institute building "IZNF". </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On the ground floor and partly in the basement of this building, on the north side </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">measuring rooms with highly sensitive measuring instruments and microscopes are set up, with which </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">experiments are carried out that tolerate no vibrations.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">For this reason, for compaction works, compaction equipment is always </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be used that works with low vibration owing to its vibration frequency; </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">excitation frequency &gt; 40 Hz.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Before the start of the construction measure a construction schedule is to be prepared by the AN, from which the </span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">approximate times for the vibration-prone works are evident.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On the basis of this construction schedule, coordination is then carried out with the responsible supervisor of the measuring facilities in the IZNF, in order to fix a time schedule acceptable to all sides for vibration-free times and times in which vibration-prone works can be carried out. The vibration-prone works are therefore to be announced with a lead time of at least 2 weeks at the IZNF, via the [FIRMA_001] and the construction supervision. The vibration-prone construction works so far in the immediate surroundings of the IZNF could, according to experience, be carried out without problems after coordination.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                  </DetailTxt>
                  <OutlineText>
                    <OutlTxt>
                      <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Low-vibration construction equipment, excitation frequency &gt; 40 Hz, poss. restrictions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                    </OutlTxt>
                  </OutlineText>
                </CompleteText>
              </Description>
            </Remark>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C13" RNoPart="1">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">[ORT_030]</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Item ID="I97" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>55</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil for excavation pit, from ground surface, loosen true to profile, store at the side, backfill, compact, with sloped walls, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">degree of compaction min. DPr 1, deformation modulus on the surface min. EV2 42 MPa,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Place of construction: excavation pit hydrant</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">total width over 4 to 5 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">total length over 5 to 6 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">excavation depth up to 1,75 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">work with equipment, with sloped walls, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Owing to the numerous utilities present in the existing ground and the confined construction field, more difficult machine excavation is as a matter of principle to be included in the price.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil excavation pit UFH loosen store backfill compact, B 4-5m L 5-6m, T up to 1,75m SU</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I98" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>30</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil for excavation pit, from ground surface, loosen true to profile, store at the side, backfill, compact, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">degree of compaction min. DPr 1, deformation modulus on the surface min. EV2 42 MPa,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">work with equipment, with sloped walls, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">width of the base over 0,8 to 0,9 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">excavation depth up to 1,75 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Owing to the numerous utilities present in the existing ground and the confined construction field, more difficult machine excavation is as a matter of principle to be included in the price.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Location: [ADRESSE_008], in which the main route of the well water pipeline also runs.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil trench supply/disposal line with equipment T up to 1,75m loosen load convey store base B 0,8-0,9m SU</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I99" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>5</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil for excavation pit, from ground surface, loosen true to profile, store at the side, backfill, compact, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">degree of compaction min. DPr 1, deformation modulus on the surface min. EV2 42 MPa,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">work by hand with sloped walls, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">width of the base over 0,8 to 0,9 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">excavation depth up to 1,75 m, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Owing to the numerous utilities present in the existing ground and the confined construction field, more difficult machine excavation is as a matter of principle to be included in the price.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Location: [ADRESSE_008], in which the main route of the well water pipeline also runs.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Manual work when exposeng within a radius of 0,5m around the obstacle.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil trench supply/disposal line by hand T up to 1,75m loosen, store at side, install, compact, base B 0,8-0,9m SU</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I100" RNoPart="4">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>20</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surplus soil, stored at the side, load onto truck of the AN, transport to the approved storage area of the AG, unload.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Waste is not hazardous, not contaminated with pollutants, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">transport distance up to 2 km, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">container size according to [PERSON_125] of the AN, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Soil load transp. truck AN up to 3km, SU</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I101" RNoPart="5">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>65</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
