                      <CompleteText>
                        <ComplTSA>Yes</ComplTSA>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Frost protection layer, load class RStO 12 Bk1,0, in ancillary and rest areas - car traffic incl. small share of heavy traffic, degree of compaction min. DPr 1,03, deformation modulus on the surface min. EV2 120 MPa, of construction material mixture for frost protection layer, recycled aggregate (RC construction material) TL Gestein, recycled aggregate [PERSON_129] 1, grading 0/45, layer thickness over 20 to 30 cm, fines content category UF 3, in the installed state max. 3 % fines, billing is by fill profiles, execution acc. to individual description, </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                          <TextComplement Kind="Owner" MarkLbl="11" ArtChrIdent="-484">
                            <ComplCaption><span>Individual description no. </span></ComplCaption>
                            <ComplBody><span> </span><br/><span>Area Immerwahrstraße carriageway </span></ComplBody>
                            <ComplTail><span/></ComplTail>
                          </TextComplement>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">.</span></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Frost protection layer Bk1,0 DPr1,03 EV2 120MPa 0/45 D 20-30cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="R30">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Edgings, built-in components</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Edgings, built-in components</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I134" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Kerb of concrete, shape TB 10/25, colour grey, used, stored at the side, with foundation and backing support on one side of concrete.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">All butt joints deviating from the straight line are to be mitre-cut.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Bedding: 20 cm  normal concrete C25/30 (LP) XF2 DIN EN 206, DIN 1045-2</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Backing wedge: vertical, thickness 10 cm continuous, on one side</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Joints: 1 cm mortar MG III</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Movement joints: spacing maximum 8 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Concrete kerb TB10/25 grey used stored at side foundation </span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">backing support C20/25 D 20cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Remark ID="R31">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surfacing works</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surfacing works</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I135" RNoPart="4">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>4</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Asphalt base course, ZTV Asphalt-StB, produce in carriageways.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Installed thickness acc. to TPD-StB by measuring with depth gauge,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the quantity of the installed mix is additionally to be proven by site-related delivery notes.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Load class:  RStO 12 Bk1,0</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">in ancillary and rest areas</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">car traffic incl. small share of heavy traffic</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Mix: AC 22 T N</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Addition of reclaimed asphalt:  possible, max. 20%</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Layer thickness: 10 cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Binder: road bitumen 50/70</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">TL Bitumen-StB and DIN EN 12591</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Edge formation: between cut edges</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Installation method: installation by hand</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Asphalt base course [PERSON_015] Bk1,0 AC22TN binder 50/70 D 10cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I136" RNoPart="5">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>4</Qty>
                    <QU>m2</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Asphalt surface course of asphalt concrete, ZTV Asphalt-StB, produce in carriageways.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Before applying the asphalt surface course, the bitu base course is to be cleaned if required and sprayed with tack coat, insofar as the contractor is responsible for the contamination.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Installed thickness acc. to TPD-StB by measuring with depth gauge,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the quantity of the installed mix is additionally to be proven by site-related delivery notes.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">In the case of a rough surface the contractor has to grit the area with bitumen-coated crushed sand and roll this in.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Load class: RStO 12 Bk1,0</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">in ancillary and rest areas</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">car traffic incl. small share of heavy traffic</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Mix: AC 8 D N</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Addition of reclaimed asphalt: not permitted</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Grading / weight: 0/11 mm - 100 kg / m2</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Impact crushing value SZ 8/12: &lt;18</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Layer thickness: single-layer - 4 cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Binder: road bitumen 50/70</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">TL Bitumen-StB and DIN EN 12591</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Installation method: installation by hand</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_015] Bk1,0 AC8DN D 4cm binder 50/70</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I137" RNoPart="6">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>4</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Construct [PERSON_016] in the thickness of the bituminous surface course with fusible bitumen sealing tape.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Before installing the surface course, clean the existing wall face, dry it as far as necessary and provide it with bituminous primer. After the primer has dried, slightly melt the joint tape on the side to be bonded and press it evenly against the wall face.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Thickness of the surface course: 4cm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Joint width: 10 mm</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_016] with sealing tape</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C19" RNoPart="4">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Hourly-rate work civil works [PERSON_132] structural works 2024</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R32">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work (daywork)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work (daywork)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Remark ID="R33">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Charge-out rates for labour</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The charge-out rates for the following wage and</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">occupational groups are to be offered without breakdown.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">They include:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- wage and salary costs,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- ancillary wage and salary costs,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- social costs including social fund contributions,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- overhead shares,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- profit.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surcharges on the charge-out rates for night, Sunday,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">public holiday and additional work (overtime) ordered by</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the client or for which the client is responsible are</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be proven separately; they are paid at the rate of the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">collective agreement.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">For night, Sunday and public holiday work, only the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">contribution to statutory accident insurance is paid as a</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">surcharge. For additional work, the social costs are</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">paid in addition.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">If the bidder employs no workers in one of the following</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">wage/occupational groups, he has to state</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">this and instead offer the deployment of workers who are</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">as equivalent as possible.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
