                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control test ZTV E-StB on special instruction of the AG for subgrade/formation level, test for deformation modulus, with dynamic plate load test TP BF-StB, execution acc. to individual description,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Individual description no.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On special instruction of the AG for the degree of compaction of the fills, to check the AN's self-monitoring. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Calibrated test equipment is to be provided by the AN.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Control test subgrade/formation deformation modulus </span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">dynamic plate load test</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I153" RNoPart="16">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>10</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <STLBBau>
                        <STLBBauCtlg>
                          <CtlgName>STLB-Bau</CtlgName>
                          <VersDate>2020-04</VersDate>
                          <WCtg>005</WCtg>
                          <Group>1817</Group>
                        </STLBBauCtlg>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>2136</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>2</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>-484</ArtChrIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>6862</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>90</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>22277</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>3</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>8318</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>1</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>10164</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>3</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Individual description no.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">On special instruction of the AG to check the AN's self-monitoring. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Medium-heavy dynamic probe acc. to DIN 4094 (tip cross-section 15 cm2), incl. travel to and from site or setting up and keeping available on site. </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The probing is to be carried out jointly with the AG's construction supervision.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dynamic probing DIN EN ISO 22476-2, for in-situ determination of the resistance of soils and soft rock to the dynamic penetration of a probe tip, termination criterion: number of blows up to 10 cm penetration depth: 3 times in succession greater than 30 or number of blows up to 10 cm penetration depth: once greater than 90, heavy dynamic probing (DPH), drilling depth up to 5 m, execution acc. to individual description.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Dynamic probing DPH</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
        <BoQCtgy ID="C20" RNoPart="6">
          <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">[PERSON_127]-other services</span><br/></LblTx>
          <BoQBody>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C21" RNoPart="1">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Documentation</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R37">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I154" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>20</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_127] well water line</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Preparation of a documentation durin the construction period by means of digital colour pictures documentation of the nodes of water lines.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photos must be assignable via the file name to the ndoe, the [PERSON_017] / the valve or the tie-in.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photos are to be filed in PDF format (max. 4 pictures on one A4 PDF) separately by the repsective construction phases/ line areas as well as the .jpg files and commented accordigly</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Per node, [PERSON_017] / valve or tie-in, one piece of photo documentation can be billed, irrespective of the number of pictures required.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photo documentation is to be handed over to the AG 2 weeks before acceptance digitally for checking on CD - 2 copies:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_127]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"> well water line</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I155" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>30</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_127] cooling line</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Preparation of a documentation durin the construction period by means of digital colour pictures documentation of the nodes of cooling lines.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photos must be assignable via the file name to the ndoe, the [PERSON_017] / the valve or the tie-in.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photos are to be filed in PDF format (max. 4 pictures on one A4 PDF) separately by the repsective construction phases/ line areas as well as the .jpg files and commented accordigly</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Per node, [PERSON_017] / valve or tie-in, one piece of photo documentation can be billed, irrespective of the number of pictures required.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The photo documentation is to be handed over to the AG 2 weeks before acceptance digitally for checking on CD - 2 copies:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_127] [PERSON_132]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I156" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>3</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">hand over as additional copy  on CD.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation as PDF file incl. photos as JPEG file, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Billed is one set of the photo documentation in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply photo documentation on data carrier CD</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I157" RNoPart="4">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_166]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">, collected in folders, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The content of the folders is to be broken down ordered by topic;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">A table of contents is to be placed in front of the content</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spines are to be labelled according to the AG's specification.The labelling of the folder spines is specified uniformly for the entire project.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">One set of the documentation is billed in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply photo documentation in [PERSON_097]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I158" RNoPart="5">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Documentation of as-built and revision drawings</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">for all [PERSON_127] trades listed in this LV</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">prepare on the basis of the assembly planning.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">System documentation and revision documents</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">consisting of:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Overview of contents</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">01.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Specialist site manager's declaration</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">02.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Approvals, welder certificates,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">03.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">EC - certificates of conformity</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">04.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Revision drawings on the basis of the assembly planning</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">05.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Drawings (final state of the work executed), </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">scale  1:25 / 1:50 / 1:250 on paper and filing in </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">06.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Records "hydraulic systems" of pressure tests,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">flushing, measured values and set values</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">07.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Copies of test certificates and manufacturer's certifs.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">08.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Records of acceptances by experts</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">09.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Photo documentation [PERSON_029] and cooling lines</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">10.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Operating and maintenance instructions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">11.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Proof of the instruction of the operating personnel</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">12.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Spare parts lists with stocking recommendation and </span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">sources of supply</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Both the paper copies and the data carriers are to be provided with dividers according to the above list. All dividers are to be created. If a divider remains empty, a sheet with the remark "not applicable" is to be filed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spine is specified uniformly for the entire project. Is a coordination with AG required.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Submission of the documentation in 1 copy 3 weeks before acceptance</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">and in 2 copies at acceptance</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The documentation documents are to be handed over to the AG 2 weeks before acceptance digitally for checking on CD - in 1 copy;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">at acceptance the checked documentation is to be handed over in 2 copies.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">CAD drawing in DWG or DXF format</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">other drawing documents in format PDF format</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Prepare system documentation and revision documents</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I159" RNoPart="6">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>3</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Product documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">hand over as additional copy  on CD.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The data carrier is to be labelled with the following details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Project name</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Content of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Date of preparation of the documentation</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Author of the doocumentation / name of the AN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply system documentation on data carrier CD</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I160" RNoPart="7">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>2</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_053]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">, collected in folders, supply and hand over.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The content of the folders is to be broken down ordered by topic;</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">A table of contents is to be placed in front of the content</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spines are to be labelled according to the AG's specification.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The folder spines are to be labelled according to the AG's specification.The labelling of the folder spines is specified uniformly for the entire project.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">One set of the documentation is billed in each case.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Supply system documentation in [PERSON_097]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I161" RNoPart="8">
                    <LumpSumItem>Yes</LumpSumItem>
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Production of the workshop and assembly planning for all pipeline construction sections listed in this LV. The fabrication and assembly drawings are to be submitted to the client in a single copy for checking three weeks before start of fabrication/assembly. In DIN A format, coloured and folded, in one folder each. Furthermore the documents are to be handed over as dwg and pdf on a CD in a single copy. In case of unclear points a clarification meeting takes place in the rooms of the project supervision.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The workshop and assembly planning is to be presented in the course of a review.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Complete with the details necessary for the assembly:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">site plans /  outdoor facilities plans,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">longitudinal and cross sections</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Collision check: For the pipe routes to be built in the project-specific traffic area, considerable obstructions of the routing by existing lines and installations such as e.g. for gas, [PERSON_029],</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">drainage, electricity, post must be expected in parts. The position</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">of these obstacles is therefore to be clarified before start of construction on the basis of</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">site plans and sectional drawings with the responsible</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">bodies and the result laid down</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">in writing. The minimum distances to existing pipe routes applicable depending on the utility or municipal</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">regulations are to be taken into account in doing so.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Preparation of a detailled construction schedule, with the following minimum details:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">order time and delivery dates for pipeline systems,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">advance planning accurate to the day,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">planning of on-site fabrication accurate to the day</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Workshop and assembly planning</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I162" RNoPart="9">
                    <LumpSumItem>Yes</LumpSumItem>
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>psch</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surveying of all pipelines ([PERSON_132], well water line), on the basis of georeferencing in the UTM grid, drawing into site plans and sections existing on data carrier interface dxf/dwg, submission on paper in triplicate, before closing of the pipe trenches and of road and path construction works, as advance document for the overall documentation, incl. recording of survey work carried out, with date of the respective pipeline sections surveyed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Note: It cannot be assumed that the pipelines can be measured completely in a single day's deployment. The cost estimate has to take the measuring in sections into account. This applies in particular to travel costs and labour effort, which are covered by this item.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surveying of the pipelines, georeferencing</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C22" RNoPart="2">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Hourly-rate work (daywork)</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R38">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Carrying out hourly-rate work against proof and at the request of the local site management. Work is paid if its execution was ordered in writing by the site management.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Only the working hours actually performed for personnel and equipment are charged. If a special [PERSON_037] is kept for the work, no payment is granted for the supervisory personnel, unless expressly agreed otherwise beforehand.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Insofar as hourly charge rates claimed are not contained in the bid, the contractor is obliged at the client's request to furnish proof of the actual labour costs on the basis of the payroll lists.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Wages above the collective agreement and ancillary labour costs are to be proven to the client on request.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Surcharges on the charge rates for night, Sunday,</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">public holiday and additional work (overtime) ordered by the client</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">or for which the client is responsible are</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">to be proven separately; they are paid in the amount of the collective</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">agreement. For night, Sunday and public holiday work, only the contribution to statutory accident insurance is paid as a surcharge. For additional work, the social costs are additionallypaid.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">All surcharges such as overheads, social contributions, accommodation allowance, travel money etc. are to be included in the hourly rate. Billing is against proof. The daywork sheets are to be signed daily by the building owner, as otherwise the wage work will not be recognised. Billing with the client has to take place promptly.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The bid total of the hourly-rate work is included in the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">bid evaluation, the hourly-rate work is</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">however not commissioned. The hourly rates offered</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">become part of the contract.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The contractor has no claim to the consumption of the hours provided for; the same charge rates apply to more or fewer hours performed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I163" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>100</Qty>
                    <QU>h</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <STLBBau>
                        <STLBBauCtlg>
                          <CtlgName>STLB-Bau</CtlgName>
                          <VersDate>2022-10</VersDate>
                          <WCtg>091</WCtg>
                          <Group>1619</Group>
                        </STLBBauCtlg>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>9088</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>8</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>10164</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>1</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>2136</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>39</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                        <STLBBauID>
                          <ArtChrIdent>11100</ArtChrIdent>
                          <ArtChIdx>0</ArtChIdx>
                          <ChVIdent>1</ChVIdent>
                        </STLBBauID>
                      </STLBBau>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Hourly-rate work by [PERSON_020] (m/f)</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">the charge-out rate for the respective worker covers all expenses such as wage and salary costs, ancillary wage and salary costs, surcharges, wage-linked and wage-dependent costs, other social costs, overheads, risk and profit.</span></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">[PERSON_020] (m/f) all costs/surcharges</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
        <BoQCtgy ID="C23" RNoPart="7">
          <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">[PERSON_151]. East - main route 2023</span><br/></LblTx>
          <BoQBody>
            <BoQCtgy ID="C24" RNoPart="1">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Piping and valves - BA 01-2023</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <PerfDescr ID="P0">
                    <PerfNo>1</PerfNo>
                    <PerfLbl>Basis of cost estimate</PerfLbl>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">All details, expenses or work listed are to be included in the price in the corresponding unit prices.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Pre-insulated bonded pipe system</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The existing pre-insulated bonded pipe system in the ground, to which the conection is to be made, is the make "isoplus".</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">DN 20 - DN 1000 with quality specification for pressure rating PN 25.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Carrier pipe with steel wall thicknesses acc. to AGFW FW 401, from wall thickness &gt; 3,2 mm bevelled ends acc. to DIN 2559/22</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- replaced by DIN EN ISO 9692-1.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Delivery length :</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Up to DN 25 in 6 m lengths, from DN 32 optionally in 6 m or 12 m lengths. This is to be determined by the contractor himself.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Casing pipe:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Polyethylene High Density (PEHD)seamless, extruded, impact- and break-resistant, acc. to DIN 8075. In accordance with EN 253, for optimum adhesion to the PUR rigid foam.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Thermal insulation:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Polyurethane rigid foam foamed without joints between carrier pipe and casing pipe. Blowing agent C- pentane, ozone depletion potential (ODP) = 0, global warming potential (GWP) = &lt; 0,001. Thermal conductivity [Lambda] maximum 0,0275 W/(mK), continuous operating temperature and foam density at least in accordance with EN 253.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The costs for welded joints on the pipe, on valves and on fittings are to be included in the price in the respective items.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The costs for necessary fitting lengths on the pipe, on valves and on fittings are to be ncluded in the price in the respective items.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Network monitoring / leak monitoring</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Copper leak warning system:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Continuous monitoring of insulated pipelines for moisture penetration, two foamed-in bare copper wires, 1,5 mm² as sensors, copper wires are wear-free, corrosion- and temperature-resistant.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The copper leak warning system is suitable for:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Extensive and branched pipe network systems with central monitoring units or measuring points, networking with automatic monitorin technology, with fully automatic monitoring and locating systems, pulse transit-time measuring technology.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The following fault types can be located manually or automatically:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- sensor wire break</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- sensor wire-pipe contact</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- moisture fault</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- [PERSON_077]</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Faults can be differentiated by type and intensity, locating accuracy is 0,2%, +/- 1 m, measuring sections can be subdivided further at any time, later route changes can be integrated into the monitoring system.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The costs for the network monitoring in the pipe, on valves and in the fittings as well as the necessary wiring work are to be included in the price in the respective items.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Note [PERSON_177] assembly guidelines</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The manufacturer-specific [PERSON_177] assembly guidelines are to be observed exactly. To avoid damage to the PE casing pipe, the pipes must not be dragged over the trench base during assembly. Rolling the pipes as well as the use of steel ropes or chains are likewise not permitted. The pipe layer is responsible for aligning the route in vertical and horizontal direction, for producing fitting lengths as well as for sliding on the connecting sockets, sealing rings and end caps.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Before welding the pipes and components, the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">corresponding connecting sockets with the associated</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">shrink sleeves must be slid onto the casing pipe, next to the</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">weld location.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Qualification of the assembly personnel</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; text-decoration:underline; font-family:Arial">Pipe joints</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Welding work is to be carried out only by welders</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">who hold a valid test certificate acc. to DIN EN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">287-1.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Welding process:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Welding process suitable for site welds specified and approved acc. to DIN EN ISO 15607, weld preparation, joint geometry on the [PERSON_089] as well as</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">distance between the pipe ends based on</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">DIN EN 448 and DIN EN ISO 9692-1, welding consumables</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">base materials matched and approved, selection and marking of welding consumables acc. to DIN EN 12536, DIN 8559 and DIN EN ISO 2560, requirement for weld seams</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">acc. to AGFW worksheet FW 401 as well as EN ISO 5817.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The joints of the black steel pipes can be gas-welded up to DN 80, but should preferably, and from DN 100 generally, be electricallywelded.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Defective welded joints are to be completely replaced by the executing trade pipeline construction. The repair of defective welds by partial replacement with new material over the defective spot or by filling the same is not permitted.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; text-decoration:underline; font-family:Arial">Insulation and sealing work</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The following services must be carried out by factory-trained and AGFW-/BFW-certified assembly personnel.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Installation, checking and recording of the IPS-Cu - network monitoring</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Producing PUR in-situ foam for insulation of joints with mobile foaming machine or hand-applied mechanically stirred foam</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Insulating and sealing of the connecting sockets at the weld locations by PUR foam and the heat treatment of the cross-linked and shrinking sealing material of the sockets as well as end or shrink caps</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Fitting expansion pads in all available shapes on expansion legs such as L-, Z- and U-bends and at all other necessary locations, according to the length and thickness details acc. to manufacturer's route plan.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Storage of pipes, fittings, accessories etc.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pipes:</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Storage level, free of stones, dry, separated by dimensions</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Sand banks, squared timbers ( 10 to 15 cm thick) serve as supports, uniform spacing of approx. 2 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Stacking height max. 2,5 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- For longer storage provide protection against weather influences, in particular UV protection and frost-free</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Accessories, small materials (sockets,caps, expansion pads etc.):</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Storage, sorted, dry, frost-free</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">- Storage of PUR foam components at approx. 15 to 25 degrees Celsius, if necessary air-conditioned room</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial">Difficulties</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Difficulties for the placing for pipelines in shored pipe trenches with bracing are to be included in the price.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Basis of cost estimate</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </PerfDescr>
                  <Item ID="I164" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <RefPerfNo IDRef="P0"/>
