            <BoQCtgy ID="C25" RNoPart="2">
              <LblTx><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt">Testing, commissioning - BA 01-2023</span><br/></LblTx>
              <BoQBody>
                <Itemlist>
                  <Remark ID="R39">
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Safety plastic jacket pipe</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Safety plastic jacket pipe</span><span style="text-align:left; font-style:italic; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Remark>
                  <Item ID="I180" RNoPart="1">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>1</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Test of the tightness of all weld seams, by means of internal air overpressure of min. 0,2 bar, soap the weld seams and visual inspection, weld seams 96 Stk, test in partial sections 75 to 100 m, recording of any leaking weld seams.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Auxiliary materials, equipment (possibly power supply), instruments necessary for ths are to be provided by the contractor and included in the price. Any waste products are to be removed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Tightness of all weld seams</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I181" RNoPart="2">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>20</Qty>
                    <QU>St</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Non-destructive weld seam test, as X-ray test, steel pipe AD 273 mm, at least 10 % of the seams are to be checked and recorded, billing by number of pieces.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Radiographic test acc. to EN 1435 with recording and evaluation acc. to DIN EN ISO 5817. This work is to be performed by a company that is specialised in this service.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The tested weld seams are to be numbered consecutively with stamped numbers. The weld seam numbers are to be stated on the films, the test certificates drawings.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Non-destructive weld seam test</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I182" RNoPart="3">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>350</Qty>
                    <QU>m</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pressure and tightness test of the cooling pipeline system, AD 273 mm, test pressure 1,3 times operating pressure  but max. 18 bar, test in partial sections 75 to 100 m, [PERSON_029] is made available on the site and is to be removed without damage after use, duration of pressure test 24 hours, falling pressure is not acceptable, pressure test with calibrated pressure recorder, pressure test before post-insulation work and covering with soil.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">The pressure tests are to be carried out in accordance with Vd TÜV 1051 or</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">DVGW worksheet 469, test procedure B1 as well as EN</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">805.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">A record of the test is to be prepared, which is to be signed by the contracttor, a responsible member of the operating staff and the project supervision.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Auxiliary materials, equipment (possibly power supply), instruments necessary for ths are to be provided by the contractor and included in the price. Any waste products are to be removed.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Pressure test cooling supply, in partial sections 75 to 100 m</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                  <Item ID="I183" RNoPart="4">
                    <UPBkdn>No</UPBkdn>
                    <Qty>21</Qty>
                    <QU>m3</QU>
                    <Description>
                      <CompleteText>
                        <DetailTxt>
                          <Text><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Filling of the pipeline sytem first construction phase with protective gas, nitrogen, filling pressure 1 bar overpressure to atmosphere, incl. filling device.</span><span style="text-align:left; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></Text>
                        </DetailTxt>
                        <OutlineText>
                          <OutlTxt>
                            <TextOutlTxt><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial">Protective gas, nitrogen, filling pressure 1 bar overpressure to atmosphere</span><span style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold; font-size:10pt; font-family:Arial"/><br/></TextOutlTxt>
                          </OutlTxt>
                        </OutlineText>
                      </CompleteText>
                    </Description>
                  </Item>
                </Itemlist>
              </BoQBody>
            </BoQCtgy>
          </BoQBody>
        </BoQCtgy>
